//? Title: AutoRec: Reconstruct Observed Ratings Without Inventing Negatives
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A warm-user autoencoder reconstructs MovieLens ratings using only training observations.
Native tensors keep missing entries out of the loss, while explicit Adam updates,
validation-only selection and fitting-only baselines expose what this short model learns.
)
\toc

> Observed ratings are different from negative preferences

A zero input means unknown or withheld, not a zero-star target. The original
U-AutoRec teaching network maps 256 normalized ratings through 32 sigmoid
units to 256 unconstrained outputs. Training minimizes squared error only at
observed fitting positions, plus 0.00005 times the two weight-matrix squared norms.
Biases are excluded from that regularizer. Predictions use only training ratings;
no validation/test target or mask enters the forward pass.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/autorec_method.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::Diagram          d(28, 1150);
  dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle style;
  style.width     = 11;
  style.height    = 5;
  style.font_size = 27;
  d.node("input", {-16, 0}, "Train-only ratings\nUnknown entries zero", style)
      .node("code", {0, 0}, "32 sigmoid units\n256 linear outputs", style)
      .node("score", {16, 0}, "Observed-only updates\nWithheld-star evaluation", style);
  d.edge("input", "code").edge("code", "score");
  d.save_svg("build/autorec_method.svg");
}
