> The actual 16,672-parameter graph

The plot traces the native forward path. A store owns encoder/W, encoder/b,
decoder/W and decoder/b; the output handles retain live derivative paths.
The model component has no optimizer, target or implicit update method.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/autorec_architecture.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  n::ParameterStore parameters(4603);
  n::Module         model(
      [&](const n::Tensor& x) { return n::models::AutoRec(parameters, x).prediction; },
      "AutoRec: 256 observed ratings to32 sigmoid units to256 predictions");
  n::ModelPlotOptions options;
  options.style    = n::ModelPlotStyle::Flow;
  options.detail   = n::ModelPlotDetail::Blocks;
  options.labels   = {.type = n::ModelPlotLabel::NameAndShape, .size = 12, .wrap = 24};
  const auto graph = model.plot(n::zeros({1, 256}), options);
  graph.save_svg("build/autorec_architecture.svg");
  if (parameters.count() != 16672 || parameters.size() != 4)
    return 1;
  std::print("{} learned scalars in{} tensors.\n", parameters.count(), parameters.size());
}
