> Original-source ratings and an explicit native partition

The checksummed original MovieLens100K archive contains100,000 ratings from943
users on1682 items. We retain users1..256 with at least10 observations among
items1..256:199 users and256 items. Per user, the native seed4601 shuffles observed
item indices, assigns floor(n/10) to validation and the next floor(n/10) to test,
and fits the rest. The resulting supports are8079/898/898. User and item IDs remain
original IDs; every prepared rating is checked against u.data. Held-out inputs
are exactly zero, while withheld targets remain available only for evaluation.

The original external preparation archive is unavailable. The manifest records
this canonical native partition and its RNG; external split or TensorFlow numerical
parity is not asserted. An existing preparation can be inspected and supplied
through the standard dataset cache. No Python preparation or external checkout is
needed. These are warm users and warm items: every retained item has fitting support.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/autorec_data.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  namespace n     = dm::nn;
  namespace m     = n::models;
  const auto root = dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("autorec");
  const auto data = m::LoadAutoRec(root);
  std::print(
      "Source{}; rows{},items{}; observed fit/validation/test{}/{}/{}.\n",
      root,
      data.input.size(0),
      data.input.size(1),
      n::sum(data.train).item(),
      n::sum(data.validation).item(),
      n::sum(data.test).item());
  const auto first   = n::slice_axis(data.ratings, 0, 0, 24),
             support = n::slice_axis(data.train, 0, 0, 24);
  auto a             = n::plot_tensor_map(first.to(n::DType::Float64), 0, 5),
       b             = n::plot_tensor_map(support.to(n::DType::Float64), 0, 1);
  a.title("Original star ratings;0 means unknown")
      .x_label("original item1..256")
      .y_label("first24 warm users");
  b.title("Fitting-only observation support")
      .x_label("original item1..256")
      .y_label("first24 warm users");
  auto layout = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2);
  layout.add(a).add(b).size(1200, 500).fit_panels().save_svg("build/autorec_data.svg");
}
