> What the short fit establishes

The executed tables report the selected model and fitting-only references on all
898 withheld ratings. A lower reconstruction loss alone does not establish a
better recommender: compare raw/clipped RMSE and MAE against the three references.
The sparse observed-rating objective avoids treating unknown entries as dislikes,
but it does not model exposure bias or solve cold start. The heatmap shows every
item for the first24 users; the printed examples follow source user/item order
without selecting attractive predictions. All arrays retain the complete199-user
outputs, masks and original identities.

> References

- Sedhain et al. (2015), [AutoRec: Autoencoders Meet Collaborative Filtering](https://doi.org/10.1145/2740908.2742726).
- GroupLens, [MovieLens100K original data and licence](https://grouplens.org/datasets/movielens/100k/).
- Native contracts: `dm::nn::models::AutoRec`, `ObservedRatingMse`, `LoadAutoRec` and `RatingErrors` in `include/datamunge/nn/autorec.hpp`.
